From: kern0x1b <kern0x1b@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Perform Web Crypto through WebKit's OpenSSL backend

The Cocoa backend works in CryptoKit, which has no armv7 Swift, so this port
uses WebKit's own OpenSSL backend: digests, HMAC, AES-GCM, CBC, CFB, CTR and key
wrapping, HKDF, PBKDF2, ECDSA, ECDH, RSA-OAEP and RSASSA-PKCS1. EC key import
reads ASN1 strings through their accessors, which OpenSSL 4 requires.
